---
layout: base.njk
---
{#- Perspectives: a case study with a methods box and three figures drawn from data, which the
    chapter template has no slot for. Same head, same .chap grid, same .stats row and .plate
    captions as every project page; the rest is scoped .psp-* in perspectives.css.

    The figures are computed at build time (src/_data/perspectivesViz.js, from perspectives.json)
    and ship as plain SVG, so they need no script and survive the homepage overlay, which lifts
    this <article> and runs none of its scripts. The stylesheet sits inside the article for the
    same reason. With no rows, each figure prints that it has nothing to draw. -#}
{%- set ch = content | chapters -%}
{%- set V = perspectivesViz -%}
{%- macro eyebrow(n, name) %}<span class="chap__eyebrow"><b>({{ n }})</b> {{ name }}</span>{% endmacro -%}
{%- macro sample() %}{% if V.sample %}<p class="psp-sample">(sample data) drawn from {{ V.sampleRows }} placeholder rows in perspectives.json, not from records. Replace them before this page is shown to anyone.</p>{% endif %}{% endmacro -%}
{%- macro empty(what) %}<div class="psp-empty" role="note"><span>(no data)</span> perspectives.json has no rows, so {{ what }} has nothing to draw. It is built from the attendance records and nothing else.</div>{% endmacro -%}
<article class="detail psp">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/perspectives.css" />
  <a class="detail__back" href="/#work">(&larr; selected work)</a>

  <span class="detail__qlabel">(research question)</span>
  <h1 class="detail__q reveal">{{ question }}</h1>
  <div class="detail__head reveal">
    <div class="detail__headtext">
      <p class="detail__sub">{{ subtitle }}</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="detail__index">
      <div><dt>(role)</dt><dd>{{ role }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>(period)</dt><dd>{{ period }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>(context)</dt><dd>{{ context }}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>(status)</dt><dd class="status">{{ status }}</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <div class="stats psp-stats reveal">
    {% for st in stats %}<div><div class="n">{{ st.n }}</div><div class="l">({{ st.l }})</div></div>{% endfor %}
  </div>

  {#- (01) the answer, first, at a size between the question and the body -#}
  <section class="chap chap--noplates psp-verdict reveal" id="ch-01">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("01", "the verdict") }}
      <div class="psp-verdict__txt">{{ ch.byNum["01"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- (02) the chain: prior, intervention, measure, result, and the revised prior pointing back at
      the first link, which is struck. Drawn by hand, not from data. -#}
  <section class="chap reveal" id="ch-02">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("02", "the hypothesis") }}
      <h2 class="chap__title">A chain, and the link that broke</h2>
      <div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["02"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="chap__pl">
      <figure class="plate psp-chain">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 860" role="img" aria-labelledby="psp-chain-t psp-chain-d">
          <title id="psp-chain-t">The hypothesis, as a chain</title>
          <desc id="psp-chain-d">Five boxes in a column. The prior: a good enough format does the work. The intervention: one fixed three-part protocol, run by many initiators, 250 plus times. What was measured: to be supplied. What came back: same protocol, different rooms; depth followed the initiator. The revised prior: the format carries the structure; whoever opens the room decides whether anyone uses it. A dashed arrow runs from the revised prior back to the first box, which is struck through.</desc>
          <defs>
            <marker id="psp-ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="psp-chain__head" /></marker>
            <marker id="psp-ah2" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="psp-chain__head2" /></marker>
          </defs>
          <g class="psp-chain__old">
            <rect x="20" y="20" width="470" height="150" />
            <text class="k" x="40" y="48">(01) the prior</text>
            <text x="40" y="82">A good enough format does the work.</text>
            <text x="40" y="108">Hand it to anyone and the room</text>
            <text x="40" y="134">goes deep.</text>
            <path class="strike" d="M38 75H418M38 101H362M38 127H146" />
            <text class="tk" x="40" y="158">TKTK · confirm this was the starting bet</text>
          </g>
          <path class="psp-chain__step" d="M255 170V214" marker-end="url(#psp-ah)" />
          <g>
            <rect x="20" y="220" width="470" height="120" />
            <text class="k" x="40" y="248">(02) the intervention</text>
            <text x="40" y="282">One fixed three-part protocol,</text>
            <text x="40" y="308">run by many initiators, 250+ times.</text>
          </g>
          <path class="psp-chain__step" d="M255 340V384" marker-end="url(#psp-ah)" />
          <g>
            <rect x="20" y="390" width="470" height="120" />
            <text class="k" x="40" y="418">(03) what was measured</text>
            <text class="tk" x="40" y="452">TKTK · what you recorded per circle</text>
            <text class="tk" x="40" y="474">that let you compare depth across rooms</text>
          </g>
          <path class="psp-chain__step" d="M255 510V554" marker-end="url(#psp-ah)" />
          <g>
            <rect x="20" y="560" width="470" height="110" />
            <text class="k" x="40" y="588">(04) what came back</text>
            <text x="40" y="622">Same protocol, different rooms.</text>
            <text x="40" y="648">Depth followed the initiator.</text>
          </g>
          <path class="psp-chain__step" d="M255 670V714" marker-end="url(#psp-ah)" />
          <g class="psp-chain__new">
            <rect x="20" y="720" width="470" height="130" />
            <text class="k" x="40" y="748">(05) the revised prior</text>
            <text x="40" y="782">The format carries the structure.</text>
            <text x="40" y="808">Whoever opens the room decides</text>
            <text x="40" y="834">whether anyone uses it.</text>
          </g>
          <path class="psp-chain__back" d="M490 785H534V95H498" marker-end="url(#psp-ah2)" />
          <text class="psp-chain__lbl" transform="translate(551 440) rotate(-90)" text-anchor="middle">replaces (01)</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="plate__cap"><span class="n">fig.01</span><span>The hypothesis as a chain. The first link is struck because the last one replaced it.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- (03) the protocol as a methods box: everything someone else would need to run a circle -#}
  <section class="chap chap--wide reveal" id="ch-03">
    <div class="chap__full">
      {{ eyebrow("03", "the protocol") }}
      <div class="psp-methods">
        <div class="psp-methods__hd"><span>(methods)</span><span>the circle, as an instrument</span></div>
        <dl class="psp-methods__dl">
          {% for p in protocol %}<div><dt>{{ p.k }}</dt><dd>{{ p.v | safe }}</dd></div>{% endfor %}
        </dl>
        <div class="psp-methods__slot">
          <span class="psp-methods__k">(verbatim · one circle, in order)</span>
          {% if prompts and prompts.length %}
          <ol>{% for q in prompts %}<li>{{ q }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>
          {% if promptsSource %}<p class="psp-methods__src">{{ promptsSource }}</p>{% endif %}
          {% else %}
          <p><span class="tk">TKTK · the prompt sequence from one real circle, verbatim, phase by phase. Set it as `prompts:` (a list) in the frontmatter, with `promptsSource:` naming the circle and date.</span></p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% if ch.byNum["03"] %}<div class="chap__body psp-methods__note">{{ ch.byNum["03"] | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- (04) findings: a claim, the evidence under it -#}
  <section class="chap chap--wide reveal" id="ch-04">
    <div class="chap__full">
      {{ eyebrow("04", "findings") }}
      {% if ch.byNum["04"] %}<div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["04"] | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
      <ol class="psp-findings">
        {% for f in findings %}
        <li>
          <span class="psp-findings__n">{{ "0" + loop.index }}</span>
          <h3 class="psp-findings__claim">{{ f.claim }}</h3>
          <p class="psp-findings__ev">{{ f.evidence | safe }}</p>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- (05) the network: people as nodes, co-attendance as ties, one panel per city -#}
  <section class="chap chap--wide reveal" id="ch-05">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("05", "the network") }}
      <h2 class="chap__title">Ties between people with no path to each other</h2>
      <div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["05"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="chap__full psp-net">
      {% if V.empty %}{{ empty("the network") }}{% else %}
      {{ sample() }}
      <div class="psp-net__panels">
        {% for P in V.network.panels %}
        {%- set ci = loop.index0 -%}
        <figure class="psp-net__panel">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ P.w }} {{ P.h }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ P.city }}: {{ P.people }} people across {{ P.circles }} circles">
            <path class="psp-tie psp-tie--prior" d="{{ P.priorPath }}" />
            <path class="psp-tie psp-tie--fresh" d="{{ P.freshPath }}" />
            {% for n in P.nodes %}{% if n.anchor %}<circle class="psp-ring" cx="{{ n.x }}" cy="{{ n.y }}" r="{{ n.r + 4 }}" />{% endif %}<circle class="psp-node psp-c{{ ci % 3 }}" cx="{{ n.x }}" cy="{{ n.y }}" r="{{ n.r }}"><title>{{ n.count }} circle{% if n.count != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% if n.anchor %} · anchor{% endif %}</title></circle>{% endfor %}
          </svg>
          <figcaption class="psp-net__name"><i class="psp-dot psp-c{{ ci % 3 }}"></i>{{ P.city }} <span>· {{ P.people }} people · {{ P.circles }} circles</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <ul class="psp-key">
        <li><i class="psp-key__fresh"></i>tie with no earlier path between the two</li>
        <li><i class="psp-key__prior"></i>tie between people already connected</li>
        <li><i class="psp-key__size"></i>size: circles attended</li>
        <li><i class="psp-key__ring"></i>anchor: {{ V.network.anchorMin }} or more circles</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="plate__cap"><span class="n">fig.02</span><span>{{ V.network.people }} people and {{ V.network.ties }} ties. {{ V.network.freshShare }}% of ties formed between two people with no earlier path between them. {{ V.network.anchors }} anchors hold {{ V.network.repeatShare }}% of all repeat attendances ({{ V.network.repeatAnchors }} of {{ V.network.repeatTotal }}).{% if V.network.crossCity %} {{ V.network.crossCity }} ties crossed cities and are not drawn; each person sits in the city where they attended most.{% endif %}</span></p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- (06) one number, set large: the system made its own operators -#}
  <section class="chap chap--noplates reveal" id="ch-06">
    <div class="chap__txt psp-repro">
      {{ eyebrow("06", "reproduction") }}
      {% if V.empty or not V.reproduction.initiators %}{{ empty("the reproduction metric") }}{% else %}
      {{ sample() }}
      <p class="psp-repro__n">{{ V.reproduction.share }}%</p>
      <p class="psp-repro__s">of the people who initiated a circle had first sat in someone else&rsquo;s.</p>
      <p class="psp-repro__f">{{ V.reproduction.fromParticipants }} of {{ V.reproduction.initiators }} initiators, read from the attendance records: an initiator counts if they attended a circle they did not run before the first one they did.</p>
      {% if V.reproduction.disagree %}<p class="psp-repro__f psp-warn">{{ V.reproduction.disagree }} {% if V.reproduction.disagree == 1 %}person is{% else %}people are{% endif %} flagged later_initiated but never initiated a circle. Check the records.</p>{% endif %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if ch.byNum["06"] %}<div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["06"] | safe }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- (07) the conversations: topics linked by shared people, clustered by theme -#}
  <section class="chap chap--wide reveal" id="ch-07">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("07", "what people talked about") }}
      <h2 class="chap__title">The conversations, as a graph</h2>
      <div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["07"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="chap__full psp-kg">
      {% if V.empty %}{{ empty("the topic graph") }}{% else %}
      {{ sample() }}
      {%- set G = V.graph -%}
      <figure class="plate">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 {{ G.w }} {{ G.h }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ G.topics }} topics and {{ G.links }} links by shared participants. The table below lists every topic.">
          {% for e in G.edges %}<line class="psp-kg__edge" x1="{{ e.x1 }}" y1="{{ e.y1 }}" x2="{{ e.x2 }}" y2="{{ e.y2 }}" stroke-width="{{ e.sw }}"><title>{{ e.w }} shared {% if e.w == 1 %}person{% else %}people{% endif %}</title></line>{% endfor %}
          {% for c in G.cats %}<text class="psp-kg__cat" x="{{ c.x }}" y="{{ c.y }}" text-anchor="middle">{{ c.cat }}</text>{% endfor %}
          {% for n in G.nodes %}<g class="psp-kg__node{% if n.major %} is-major{% endif %}"><circle cx="{{ n.x }}" cy="{{ n.y }}" r="{{ n.r }}"><title>{{ n.name }} · {{ n.cat }} · {{ n.circles }} circle{% if n.circles != 1 %}s{% endif %} · {{ n.people }} people · {{ n.cities }}</title></circle>{% if n.label %}<text x="{{ n.x }}" y="{{ n.y + n.r + 22 }}" text-anchor="middle">{{ n.name }}</text>{% endif %}</g>{% endfor %}
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="plate__cap"><span class="n">fig.03</span><span>{{ G.topics }} topics across {{ V.circles }} circles. A line joins two topics that shared at least one participant; its weight is how many. Size is the number of circles on that topic.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <details class="psp-table">
        <summary>(every topic, as a table)</summary>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>topic</th><th>theme</th><th>circles</th><th>people</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{% for t in G.table %}<tr><td>{{ t.name }}</td><td>{{ t.cat }}</td><td>{{ t.circles }}</td><td>{{ t.people }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
        </table>
      </details>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- (08) photographs: a restrained grid. A slot with no `src` stays a striped frame. -#}
  <section class="chap chap--wide reveal" id="ch-08">
    <div class="chap__full">
      {{ eyebrow("08", "photographs") }}
      <div class="chap__body psp-consent">{{ ch.byNum["08"] | safe }}</div>
      <div class="psp-photos">
        {% for p in photos %}
        <figure class="plate">
          <div class="plate__img{% if not p.src %} psp-slot{% endif %}">{% if p.src %}<img src="{{ p.src }}" alt="{{ p.alt or '' }}"{% if p.w and p.h %} width="{{ p.w }}" height="{{ p.h }}"{% endif %} loading="lazy" />{% endif %}</div>
          <figcaption class="plate__cap"><span class="n">fig.{{ "0" + (loop.index + 3) }}</span><span>{{ p.cap | safe }}</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- The product screens: small and late, one line, not a section of their own -#}
  <aside class="psp-software reveal" aria-label="the software">
    <p>The instrument got software so it could run without us. <span class="tk">TKTK · one sentence on what the software did (sign-up, matching, reminders?), and its name if it had one</span></p>
    <div class="psp-software__screens">
      {% for s in (screens or [{}, {}]) %}
      <figure class="plate"><div class="plate__img{% if not s.src %} psp-slot{% endif %}">{% if s.src %}<img src="{{ s.src }}" alt="{{ s.alt or '' }}"{% if s.w and s.h %} width="{{ s.w }}" height="{{ s.h }}"{% endif %} loading="lazy" />{% endif %}</div>{% if not s.src %}<figcaption class="plate__cap"><span class="tk">TKTK · screen {{ loop.index }}</span></figcaption>{% endif %}</figure>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </aside>

  <section class="chap chap--noplates reveal" id="ch-09">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("09", "what failed") }}
      <div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["09"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chap chap--noplates reveal" id="ch-10">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("10", "ethics") }}
      <div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["10"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chap chap--noplates reveal" id="ch-11">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("11", "open questions") }}
      <div class="chap__body psp-questions">{{ ch.byNum["11"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chap chap--noplates reveal" id="ch-12">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("12", "lineage") }}
      <div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["12"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chap chap--noplates reveal" id="ch-13">
    <div class="chap__txt">
      {{ eyebrow("13", "credits") }}
      <div class="chap__body">{{ ch.byNum["13"] | safe }}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if next %}
  <a class="detail__next reveal" href="/#work">
    <span class="lbl">(next)</span>
    <span class="nm">{{ next }}</span>
    <span style="color:var(--accent)">&rarr;</span>
  </a>
  {% endif %}
</article>
